{{!
    @template tool_vae/declare_page

    The page that declares an activity, under its title: the notifications (a refusal, the records hidden, the competencies
    off...), the sentence that says the text is kept, the way to position oneself, a fold per record declared on with the
    panel "where am I", the text given back when there is no form, and the form. Each part only when the state has it.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\declare_page. The template holds no logic.
    Every value is escaped (double braces) except these keys:
    * noticehtml - a notification drawn by the renderer of the core
    * panelhtml - the panel drawn by the template tool_vae/whereami_tree
    * kepthtml - the text given back, drawn by the template tool_vae/kept_text ('' when nothing)
    * formhtml - the form of the declaration, drawn by moodleform::render() ('' when no form)

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * notices - array of {noticehtml}
    * keptnote - object or null: text, the sentence that says what was written is kept
    * others - array of {noticehtml}, the records hidden, after that sentence
    * selfpos - object or null: url and text, the way to position oneself
    * panels - array of {summary, panelhtml}
    * kepthtml - string, HTML of a template
    * formhtml - string, HTML of the core

    Example context (json):
    {
        "notices": [{"noticehtml": "<div class=\"alert alert-danger\">The record is hidden.</div>"}],
        "keptnote": {"text": "What you wrote is kept in the form below."},
        "others": [{"noticehtml": "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">Another record is hidden.</div>"}],
        "selfpos": {"url": "https://example.com/admin/tool/vae/selfposition.php?userid=7", "text": "Position myself"},
        "panels": [{"summary": "Where I stand on RNCP100", "panelhtml": "<section class=\"tool-vae-whereami\"></section>"}],
        "kepthtml": "",
        "formhtml": "<form action=\"#\"></form>"
    }
}}
{{#notices}}{{{noticehtml}}}{{/notices}}{{#keptnote}}<p>{{text}}</p>{{/keptnote}}{{#others}}{{{noticehtml}}}{{/others}}{{!
}}{{#selfpos}}<p><a href="{{url}}">{{text}}</a></p>{{/selfpos}}{{!
}}{{#panels}}<details class="mb-3"><summary>{{summary}}</summary>{{{panelhtml}}}</details>{{/panels}}{{!
}}{{{kepthtml}}}{{{formhtml}}}
